# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 2 (plan §3 :245 (а)): the author's example -- a bare `Counter` at
# the root executes the named Structure, its whole body (Q19.2 = 2): the declaration stores its
# initializer again, the statement runs.  Construction ran none of it (book :928): Counter\n reads 0
# before the first execution, 1 after it and 1 after the second -- 2 if the declaration did not run
# again.  The last state stays in the field (book :1094).  Was unit_bare_struct_refused ("executing a
# named Structure is not supported yet").  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 1U
return
size_t: before 9U
before: Counter\n
Counter
size_t: once 9U
once: Counter\n
Counter
size_t: twice 9U
twice: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: before = 0U && once = 1U && twice = 1U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
